# Story 21: Pane Groups & Lanes (45s)
# Hook: Beneath every layout is a tree -- lanes hold groups, groups hold panes.
# Duration: 45s
# Source: story-021-pane-groups-lanes.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 6

[00:00.0 --> 00:04.0]
Beneath every layout is a tree -- lanes hold groups, groups hold panes.

[00:04.0 --> 00:14.0]
Start rysh and split right a couple of times. Each column you create is a pane group with its own flex weight.

[00:14.0 --> 00:23.0]
Switch to rysh mode and run ##pg list -- short for panegroup -- to see every group in the tab and its flex share.

[00:23.0 --> 00:32.0]
##pg info zooms in on the group holding the active pane.

[00:32.0 --> 00:40.0]
Lanes are the rows of columns that tile your tab. ##lane list shows them, with the panes they contain.

[00:40.0 --> 00:45.0]
Lanes, groups, panes -- a tidy hierarchy you can inspect any time from rysh mode.

